 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Of course. Are you thinking of something she can share, like a big tray bake in the oven, or something she can cook on the stove? The basics are usually fine, like baked chicken, roasts, mashed potatoes and vegetables. Read the ingredients and check for gluten free labels. Then she'll need to be careful with toppings too. A simple tomato pasta sauce is usually fine, while hummus or garlic sauce can contain gluten. Sushi is one of the easiest because there's nothing to mix, just rolls.",
